    "narrative": "With the fantasy season winding down on September 29th, the Austin Waves must prioritize high-floor production to manage our remaining game caps. Our most reliable play today is **Sam Antonacci**, who leads the board with a score of 54.47. He benefits from a favorable matchup against Blubaugh (4.04 xERA) and occupies the leadoff spot, providing the volume necessary to hunt stolen bases\u2014our scarcest category. **Jackson Merrill** (54.01) remains a high-priority start despite facing a lefty in Matthew Boyd; while his dynamic platoon split is negative, his role in the heart of the order and his consistent base-running upside against a moderate SP keep him safely in our outfield rotation.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involved the marginal grouping of **Drake Baldwin** (48.14) and **Heliot Ramos** (47.81). While **Drake Baldwin** faces a formidable arm in Luzardo, his leadoff placement grants him extra plate appearance potential that outweighs his mediocre efficiency score. Conversely, **Heliot Ramos** sits right on the cusp of our bench threshold; while he faces the lefty Tolle, his score is bolstered by his batting order position, making him a superior option to the inactive **Luis Robert Jr.** (IL) or our currently idle core of **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson**. We are carefully monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Heliot Ramos**; should official lineups shuffle these players into lower-leverage spots, we are prepared to pivot to the bench to preserve our caps. No major weather risks are flagged, but the concentration of lefty-heavy matchups for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos** against Tolle requires disciplined monitoring of in-game defensive substitutions that could limit their total volume.",
